From aa6c7efa179dbc77054e1dfbad00e0e98f2f4069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 07:31:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] assurance.machinery: safety software identity, intervention,
 and the staleness join
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WHY
  Machinery Regulation (EU) 2023/1230 applies 20 January 2027. Annex III 1.1.9
  requires a machine to identify its safety-relevant software and record
  evidence of intervention in it. Nobody can do either today. And the piece
  that is worth more than either: a change to safety software silently
  invalidates the validation that preceded it, and no product on the market
  can tell you which validation, or when.

WHAT
  src/assurance/machinery/manifest.py     what is on the machine, hash by hash,
                                           with the provenance of every hash
  src/assurance/machinery/divergence.py   whether it still matches the
                                           configuration it was CE-marked with
  src/assurance/machinery/intervention.py who changed what, who authorised it,
                                           what was re-run
  src/assurance/machinery/staleness.py    THE JOIN: which safety functions still
                                           have evidence that describes the
                                           machine as it is today
  src/assurance/machinery/record.py       sealing into the ledger; the passport
  src/assurance/machinery/cli.py          record-manifest / record-change / diff
                                           / coverage / passport / check
  src/assurance/api/machinery_routes.py   six endpoints, two of them free
  examples/machinery/                     a cell whose firmware was swapped
                                           without the version string moving
  deploy/assurance/MACHINERY.md           what it does and what it will not say

  src/assurance/machine/bundle.py         a verification now carries the time of
                                           the run it describes, and may be
                                           sealed under a machine key

CUSTOMER VALUE
  "SF-01 protective stop — STALE. Last verified 9 February; invalidated by
  INT-0007 on 14 March, which changed the safety controller firmware and re-ran
  nothing. The cell has run 183 days on a validation that stopped describing
  it." No integrator, insurer or plant manager has ever been handed that
  sentence, and every one of them needs it before January 2027.

RISK
  The inference must never over-claim, so every link is declared by the customer
  and visible in the output. A function with no declared checks reports
  not_demonstrable, never covered. An item with no hash reports uncomparable,
  never unchanged. A verification is dated by the run, not by the filing. And
  every assessment states that it cannot confirm the manifest is complete: an
  item nobody listed is covered by nothing here and reported by nothing here.

ROLLBACK
  git revert this commit. Outside assurance/machinery it touches bundle.py
  (two additive fields), plans.py (one free quota and copy), deps usage,
  one router, one CLI domain, one ruff ignore.

TESTS
  400 passed (80 new), ruff clean over src/assurance and the new tests.
  The end-to-end case — a March firmware change stranding a February sign-off —
  is tested through the real ledger, not a stub.

SUCCESS CONDITION
  One integrator runs `machinery coverage` on a cell they believed was signed
  off, finds a stale safety function, and cannot unsee it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
